{"kind":"stack","id":"stk-forces-1","title":"Forces: contact and magnets","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"magnet"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Which force can pull two objects together without touching them?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Magnetic force","why":"Magnets pull on each other across a gap, without contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Friction","why":"Friction needs surfaces to rub together, so it needs contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Push from your hand","why":"A hand push only works when you touch the object.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Contact force"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A force that only acts when two objects touch each other."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"A football is kicked. What must happen for the kick to move it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The boot must touch the ball","why":"A kick is a contact force, so the boot must touch the ball.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The boot must be near the ball","why":"Pupils may think closeness is enough, but kicks need contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The ball must be heavier than the boot","why":"Weight does not decide whether a kick needs contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Non-contact force"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-e","content":"A force that acts between objects that are not touching, such as magnetism."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"A magnet is held above a paperclip, not touching it. The paperclip moves. Which force did that?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Magnetic force","why":"Magnetic force acts across a gap, so the paperclip moves without contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Friction","why":"Friction needs the surfaces to touch, and here nothing touches.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Air pushing it","why":"Air is too weak to move a paperclip like that.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You find a box of magnets and a box of rubber bands. Which box do you open first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"The magnets","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"The rubber bands","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The magnets pull a key across the table, with no touching. You smile and tidy up the box."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"You stretch a rubber band between your fingers. It only moves when you pull it, by touch."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which pair of objects can attract each other without touching?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Two magnets held apart","why":"Magnets attract across a gap, so they need no contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Two wooden blocks on a table","why":"Blocks only push when they touch, so this needs contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"A pencil and a rubber","why":"Pencil and rubber only move each other when touching.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"A tug of war rope is pulled. Which force needs contact?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"The pull of the hands on the rope","why":"The hands must touch the rope to pull it, so this is contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"The pull of a magnet on the rope","why":"A magnet pulls across a gap, so it is not contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"The pull of gravity on the rope","why":"Gravity acts at a distance, so it is not contact.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished forces: contact and magnets!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. Some forces need touching and some work across a gap."}],"actions":[]}}
